A||||9||Mach10||My First Autocross (*squee!*)||||10||
Z||000000||Mach10||10-09-2001||09:05 PM||||Yesterday, last day of the season, my buddy Ian finally convinces me to try out my car. What the hell. I pay the dues, and borrow a helmet. <P>I swear to GOD that it is the most fun you can have in a car (with clothes on)!<P>After having my car teched, and finding out my balljoints are going (they were fine LAST month  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> ), they finally let me on with a warning to abort if the car started handling funny. Apparantly cutting people out of flipped cars isn't so fun.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"> I go get my number. "2." I'm second up. Great, so I have no idea how this course works. I was busy getting my car tech'd and missed most of the walkaround.<P>My first run taught me a lot about my car. Long wide circles are not as friendly to the car as sharp hard corners. The car felt GREAT. Too bad I missed a sort of hidden gate (It was off to the side, in a big cluster of pylons) and O/C'd. found out that the route back could be taken FAST  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Unfortunately, I was nowhere near the marshals, so I didn't know which gate I had missed. I swore to keep an eye out for it...<P>Second run was a little better. Got a better start, layed out some good rubber on the corners I felt comfy with. Whipped around the hairpin wall, hit the skidpad hard and fast (and ploughed the car halfway to china &gt;:\ ) and barrelled down the slalom, full throttle. On one zig, The rear broke out, so I slacked the gas to snap it back. Which it did, nicely. Too bad I tromped on the gas too hard, too soon, and the rear flipped out the OTHER way. Full 270 spinout, onto the gravel. Missed every damn cone! I airplane looped, and carried on. Same damn gate missed. ARRG! <P>Now it was MY turn to marshall. We had about 40 cars out, and broken into 2 sections. I was first section, and had 2 runs. So I wandered out to the toughest section to try and figure out wtf I was doing wrong. A peppy MR2 comes blazing out of the corner, and manages to get the gate I'd missed, and blasts through the wall. Then he got lost and spent another 15 seconds driving around in circles trying to find the next gate. No such luck, he drives straight back. Saw some nifty cars out. Some guy was driving his XJS V-12. That was some ****  watching this driver man-handle that 4700# 385Hp beast around the track. He was good! Around the wide apex, he lost the rear, and just jammed the throttle. Best looking smokeshow I've ever seen. A jag rolling backwards, rear tires a blur, making a HUGE smokescreen. On his next run, he did the most spectaculare spinout of the meet, a great oversteer through the slalom, 180 spin taking out 3 whole gates. <BR> <P>My turn again! I knew what to do this time, but took it fairly easy. Tail flying out on the big turns, frontend pushing out on the tighties. Trip the gates for a flawless run at 58.9. <P>Take another run, and this time, I just FLOGGED the Bunsen Burner. Found a perfect raceline around the apex, dropped the throttle, came out of the corner sideways, pointing RIGHT at the next gate. Opened it up, and cruised through for a best time of 57.1<P>Learned a lot about how  the car drives. I also learned that AutoX is VERY hard on alread worn out ball joints. Need to have those done soon. Best part? I wasn't last! something like 25-30th or so out of 35-40? I reached my goal: A TIME, not just O/Cs  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I heartily recommend at least ONE autocross race. Lotsa fun.<P>Met up with 3400Fiero at the track, and looked over his TDC swap. He agreed to help me with the wiring on mine. Sweet. Best time was by a Honda S2000. The driver was awesome. Even beat out the FormulaV||||reg||10
Z||000001||AutoXdbdragSE||10-09-2001||11:45 PM||||Autocrossing fieros is so cool..  it's amazing how suprised people will be when you get good.. fieros are DAMN fast autocross cars.. i have an 84 se with the 4.10, and on street tiers i was the 5th fastest at my last autocross..just ask Jefrysuko how fast an 84 fiero can be..  enjoy your fiero, you will soon be living autocross.. especialy when you start beating vettes.. they get really pissed at you when you beat them with only 92 hp.. hehe||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||10-10-2001||12:00 AM||||I got the Se v6, so it comes out the corners nice...||||reg||10
Z||000003||sqoach||10-10-2001||12:08 AM||||Sweet! I want to take my car out on a course some day. My favorite rides at amusement parks are the go-carts!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I'm really good at those. Sliding around corners (with the ones that are fast enough) is fun  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Of course I'm sure it's much harder with a real car. Main thing I'm scared of is wrecking my car. But it'd be fun. I always watch the autocrossing on ESPN when I can. Vette, Porsche, Audi, BMW, Viper, NSX. It's cool.<BR>How much does that usually cost? I'm sure I can save up some money if need be. Sounds like a lot of fun!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">            <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*SOLD*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC</FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000004||Mach10||10-10-2001||12:27 AM||||Well, for me, it was $20 for the race. Next year, because I will be a full member, it will be 175 for the year (11 races, discount at some "open track" events). I wasn't at all worried about the car. It's a large parking lot (fairground, actually, off season) with a cone-setup. The cones leave nasty markings though. Like black shoes on a gym floor. A few minutes with a good car shampoo and a soft cloth fixes it a treat, as does a Mother's Clay Bar. <P>As I said, some really cool wipeouts, NO damage to any car (except that I wore out my ball joints even more  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> ). Lots of fun!||||reg||7
Z||000005||sloth85GT||10-10-2001||01:02 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I'm so much more upset, why did you have to post that? I REALLY REALLY REALLY wanted to go, but I was flat broke, now I have to wait until May???? DAMMIT!!! I wanna go noooowwwwwww. Oh well, I'm glad you had fun Sean, I'm definately going to get a season pass next year, I didn't even know that we held AutoX events here. So I should go wipe my tears away now, this is depressing.....<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">     <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ferrari_cdn||10-10-2001||01:47 AM||||And I was supposed to be THERE!  Of all the days my starter decided to give me the finger.<P>I stopped at my girlfriend's to help her get online with the uiversity library thingy and then Ice wouldn't start.  After ****ing with it for a while she finally started but I chose to go home in case she won't start when I'm there.<P>There's always next year.  But the wait...missing Mach10's first race...damn.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ferrari_cdn" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ferrari_cdn.JPG">  </A>  <BR>AIM: CanadianFiero||||reg||8
Z||000007||Tonker||10-10-2001||01:03 PM||||Great stuff! Congrats Mach.  Is there anywhere that I can learn more about autocross? Never heard of it before, except in passing.||||reg||5
